  "description": "GUZJIV crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 2 m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H120 Cr4 Dy4 N16 O28,3(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1C (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Cr1B (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr1A (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr1C (Cr) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.333-4.034 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.70-113.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cr4Dy4(μ3-OH)4(μ-N3)4(mdea)4(piv)4]·3CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
